WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:07.380
Speaker 1: The arrests continue for people
involved in the January 6th Trump riots.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:14.179
And the Justice Department has now charged
a soldier in the Wisconsin National Guard

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:17.220
for his involvement in the insurrection.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:25.000
On January 6th, Abraham Markovsky and an associate
report, CNN allegedly traveled to Washington,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.250
D.C., together to attend Trump's protest against
the certification of the 2012 election after

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.310
the rally.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:37.500
Investigators say Markovsky and his associate
walked to the Capitol, spent 40 minutes inside

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.500
the building.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.870
Markovsky has been charged with four federal
crimes, including violent entry or disorderly

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:44.870
conduct.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.989
As of this morning, he has not yet entered
a plea.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:53.170
Markovsky is one of the nearly three dozen
current or former service members charged

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:57.850
in connection with the January 6th attack,
says CNN.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:01.030
Based on a review of Pentagon records and
court documents.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:05.930
The majority are veterans, including many
who served in Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:13.810
But Markovsky is part of a smaller group in
that he is, or at least was, a current member

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.840
of the military.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.260
This is not hugely shocking.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.590
In the immediate aftermath of the January
6th Trump riots, we knew that there was not

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.530
only a military presence but a law enforcement
presence.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:31.560
I'm not saying to defend the capital there
was that, but I'm saying in terms of the perpetrators

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:40.930
and now we are learning more about the specifics
of this overrepresentation in the group of

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:47.040
writers in the defendants charged with their
involvement on January 6th.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.540
Military and law enforcement are overrepresented,
although not by as much as it may be looked

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.160
like earlier on.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:02:00.800
Now, this action by Markovsky seems to be
in violation, not just a federal law, but

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.350
also of the National Guard oath.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:07.049
It looks like it's in violation of an article
banning mutiny and sedition.

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:12.370
The National Guard oath says, I solemnly swear
that I will support and defend the constitution

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:18.670
of the US and of the state of whatever, because
National Guards or state National Guards against

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:22.540
all enemies, foreign and domestic, I will
bear true faith and allegiance to them, and

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:27.250
I will obey the orders of the president of
the United States and the governor of whatever

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:33.430
state and the orders of the officers appointed
to me according to law and regulations, clearly

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:37.750
a violation by participating in the riot of
the National Guard oath.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:43.450
But then also looking at Article ninety four
on Mutiny and sedition, any person subject

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:51.360
to this chapter who with intent to usurp or
override lawful military authority, refuses

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:57.599
in concert with any other person to obey orders
or otherwise do his duty or creates any violence

00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:02.300
or disturbance is guilty of mutiny.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:07.550
That is exactly what the January 6th riots
were about.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:14.190
So although the charges so far are just federal,
I'm seeing significant reason that there should

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:20.960
be charges here under the US Code of Military
Justice as well, at least for this individual,

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.600
if not for others as well.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.780
Now, in terms of, you know, consequences and
penalties, it's just too early.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:32.000
There are certainly people who are going to
do some jail time for their participation

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.500
in the January 6th riots.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:38.250
Many are going to plead out and we just have
to wait and see.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:45.020
But we're continuing to see active service
members charged in they're involved for their

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:47.190
involvement in the January 6th riots.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:50.390
Let me know what you expect as far as sentencing
on some of these.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:55.020
Will being a member of the military be an
aggravating factor in sentencing or will it

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.230
be a mitigating factor in sentencing?

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:58.519
If indeed we get to that point?

00:03:58.519 --> 00:03:59.519
Let me know.

00:03:59.519 --> 00:04:01.670
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:05.549
We have a perfect, perfect show for you today.

00:04:05.549 --> 00:04:22.129
Glad you're 

00:04:22.129 --> 00:05:29.539
with us.

